{"attempt":3,"diagnostics":[],"encoding":"verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1","feedback":["CRITIC DIAGNOSTIC REPAIR: Refine the third gap: conditional state selection is expressible using the registered list operations. For accumulator sort S, construct a singleton list containing the proposed updated state, filter it with a quantifier-free scalar guard via decide, and fold the resulting list with initial state equal to the old state and body var index 0. A true guard returns the updated state; a false guard preserves the old state. Thus absence of an explicit conditional term does not independently prevent guarded previous-value updates. Retain every active obligation ID and the precise string-ordering, integer-bounded list-generation, and nullable integer payload-extraction gaps. This conditional construction does not extract an Int from result(error=Unit,ok=Int), generate arbitrary bucket indices, or compare arbitrary strings lexicographically, so it does not supply a complete implementation or justify weakening the request."],"milestone_authority":false,"phase":"formalize","results":[{"agent":"critic","checked":null,"instance":"critic/formalize/3/R0/group-1/critic/1","proposal":{"corrections":[{"artifact":"formalization.json","diagnostic_index":0,"explanation":"Refine the third gap: conditional state selection is expressible using the registered list operations. For accumulator sort S, construct a singleton list containing the proposed updated state, filter it with a quantifier-free scalar guard via decide, and fold the resulting list with initial state equal to the old state and body var index 0. A true guard returns the updated state; a false guard preserves the old state. Thus absence of an explicit conditional term does not independently prevent guarded previous-value updates. Retain every active obligation ID and the precise string-ordering, integer-bounded list-generation, and nullable integer payload-extraction gaps. This conditional construction does not e